#~ msgid ""
#~ "A rectified stereo pair observes the "
#~ "same point from two positions. Once "
#~ "the epipolar lines are horizontal, the"
#~ " horizontal coordinate difference of the"
#~ " match is the disparity :math:`d`, "
#~ "and depth follows from the rectified "
#~ "geometry:"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ ":math:`f_x` is the rectified focal "
#~ "length, :math:`T_x` the baseline component "
#~ "along the camera x axis, and "
#~ ":math:`c_{x1}, c_{x2}` the horizontal "
#~ "principal points of the two rectified"
#~ " views. Setting :math:`d_{offs} = 0` "
#~ "is only correct when the two views"
#~ " happen to share a principal point;"
#~ " otherwise the whole cloud shifts "
#~ "sideways by :math:`d_{offs} Z / f_x`."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "_`Stage 1: rectification`"
#~ msgstr "使用演示"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "``stereoRectify`` produces ``R1``, ``R2``, "
#~ "``P1``, ``P2`` and ``Q``; "
#~ "``initUndistortRectifyMap`` turns those into a"
#~ " map pair per camera, and ``remap``"
#~ " resamples the images. Three details "
#~ "matter:"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "``alpha`` trades coverage for resolution. "
#~ "``alpha = 0`` keeps every source "
#~ "pixel and changes the focal length, "
#~ "so the depth equation must use the"
#~ " rectified :math:`f_x`, not the original"
#~ " one."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The common ROI of the two views"
#~ " is cropped away, and ``Q``'s fourth"
#~ " column plus the principal points of"
#~ " ``P1``/``P2`` are rebased onto the "
#~ "crop. A crop is a translation of"
#~ " the origin."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Remapping a white image with the "
#~ "same maps yields the pixels that "
#~ "really carry data; without that mask "
#~ "the matcher reads the black border "
#~ "as scene content and produces spurious"
#~ " disparity there."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "``cv::StereoSGBM`` runs on the gray "
#~ "images, padded left and right so "
#~ "the search window never runs off "
#~ "the image. It reports 1/16 px "
#~ "fixed point with ``(minDisparity - 1)"
#~ " * 16`` marking \"no match\". The "
#~ "pipeline unpacks to float, drops values"
#~ " outside the configured window, and "
#~ "checks left-right consistency with a "
#~ "bilinear sample of the right-view "
#~ "map at :math:`x - d`."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "_`Stage 3: depth and cloud`"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Depth is computed per pixel with "
#~ "the equation above; NaN marks pixels "
#~ "without a valid measurement. The point"
#~ " cloud back-projects with the pinhole"
#~ " model in the rectified left camera"
#~ " frame:"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "X = \\frac{(u - c_x) Z}{f_x}, "
#~ "\\qquad Y = \\frac{(v - c_y) "
#~ "Z}{f_y}, \\qquad Z = Z"
#~ msgstr ""

